# Cloudflare Pages routing, copied verbatim into build/ by SvelteKit.
#
# A missing hashed build asset must 404 for real, never fall back to the SPA
# shell: `_headers` marks /_app/immutable/* cached forever (`immutable`), and
# once a fallback 200 HTML response gets edge-cached under that header it
# sticks around for up to a year — a stale client requesting one dead chunk
# once is enough to poison that URL for every visitor afterwards, on any
# deployment, until the cache is purged. A 404 status isn't eligible for that
# caching, so this can't happen again. Every other unmatched path is a
# client-side route and still needs the SPA shell, so a hard refresh on e.g.
# /learn keeps working.
/_app/immutable/*  /404.html  404
/*                 /index.html  200
